Field-of-View Layout
--------------------------------------------------------------


   IIRS Field-of-View:
   ---------------------
                      
   
   .      FOV     .  ^

   |`.   .-.    .'|  |

   |  `.'   ` .'  |  |

   |    `.  .'    |  |

   |      `'      | 75 mm

   |    .'  `.    |  |

   |  .'      `.  |  |

   |.'          `.|  |

   `--------------'  v

   |<- -15 mm- -->|


                         15 mm      
        FOV =     ( ATAN ----- )  = 11.44 deg.
                         75 mm 
   >From the 100 km altitude of Chandrayaan-2 S/C, an fov angle of 11.44 deg provides a footprint of 20 km on the lunar surface. (FWHM angle 5.72 deg). 


FOV Definitions
--------------------------------------------------------------

This section defines the FOV. These definitions are based on the IIRS detector parameters provided in a format consistent with/required by the SPICe(CSPICE) function GETFOV (getfov_c). 
Mandatory key words if GETFOV will be used, are, INS-152240_FOV_FRAME, INS-152240_FOV_SHAPE and INS-152240_BORESIGHT.
 
 Here, the X axis of the instrument IIRS is along the boresight (i.e 90 deg to the lunar surface). FOV_REF_ANGLE for IIRS is 0 degrees from the X axis. FOV_CROSS_ANGLE is  +/-5.72 degrees.
                                   
                             Y        
                             ^
                             | (X axis is into this plane)           
           Z  <--------------x ------------->-Z
                             |            
					  -Y

                          
       
where the FOV_REF_VECTOR keyword specifies a reference
vector that, together with the boresight vector, define the plane in which the half angle given in the FOV_REF_ANGLE keyword is measured. The other half angle given in the FOV_CROSS_ANGLE keyword is measured in the plane normal to this plane and containing the boresight vector


Camera Optics Parameters
--------------------------------------------------------
 
   The following table summarizes IIRS detector optics parameters:
 
      Camera           Focal Length, mm     Aperture, mm       F number
      -------------------------------------------------------------------
      I                     75                  30              2.5
      -------------------------------------------------------------------

   These values are incorporated in the keywords below. focal lengths and aperture are converted to meters.

      \begindata

      INS-152240_FOCAL_LENGTH = ( 75.0 ) 
      INS-152240_APERTURE     = ( 30.0 )
      INS-152240_F_NUMBER     = ( 2.5 )
      
      \begintext

Camera Detector Parameters
--------------------------------------------------------
 
   The following table summarizes IIRS detector parameters. As these data show the detectors are all line arrays.
 
      Camera                 Lines      Pixels    Pixel Size, microns
      ---------------------------------------------------------------
      I                        256         500             30
      ---------------------------------------------------------------

   These values are incorporated in the keywords below; pixel sizes 
   are converted to meters.

      \begindata

      INS-152240_PIXEL_SAMPLES  = ( 500        )
      INS-152240_PIXEL_LINES    = ( 256           )
      INS-152240_CENTER         = ( 249.5, 0.5 )       
      INS-152240_PIXEL_SIZE     = ( 0.00003    )

      \begintext

Camera FOV Definitions
--------------------------------------------------------

   This section defines the field of view (FOV) for each detector, using a
   rectangular shape.

   The FOVs are defined with respect to the corresponding camera frames.

      \begindata

	 INS-152001_PLATFORM_ID        = ( -152001 )
         INS-152240_FOV_CLASS_SPEC       = 'ANGLES'
         INS-152240_FOV_SHAPE            = 'RECTANGLE'
         INS-152240_FOV_FRAME            = 'CH2_IIRS_I'
         INS-152240_BORESIGHT            = ( 1.0, 0.0, 0.0 )
         INS-152240_FOV_REF_VECTOR       = (0.0, 1.0, 0.0 )
         INS-152240_FOV_REF_ANGLE        = ( 0.0 )
         INS-152240_FOV_CROSS_ANGLE      = ( 5.72 )
         INS-152240_FOV_ANGLE_UNITS      = ( 'DEGREES' )

      \begintext

End of the IK file.

